    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/vKEsyHFk#FlAhpGUe",
      "title": "Agent work has a lifetime of its own",
      "narrative": "The Archboard server owns a private Codex child in its own process group. Sign-in, config and threads live in one Codex home that every Archboard server on this machine shares. Each browser tab has its own conversation: a workhorse that does the work, and a coordinator that voice talks to. A reload keeps the conversation. A minute after a tab closes, its conversation ends, and Codex unloads its threads once no work runs on them. When the child exits, each tab starts a new conversation with its next message. The threads author boards through the CLI, like any agent.",
